.TH DQL-SERVER 1 "2026-07-05" "dql 0.1.0" "DelightQL Manual"
.SH NAME
dql-server \- serve the DelightQL relay protocol on a Unix socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dql server
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a relay-protocol server on a Unix domain socket. On startup the
socket path is printed alone on the first stdout line (convenient for
scripts), followed by a human-readable status line naming the worker
count, database, and timeouts. This is the execution backend used by
the test-ball runner.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Unix socket path. Default:
.IR /tmp/dql\-{pid}.sock .
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Number of worker threads. Default 0 = available CPUs.
.TP
.BI \-\-idle\-timeout " SECONDS"
Shut down after N seconds with no messages. 0 (default) disables.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket\-idle\-timeout " SECONDS"
Shut down after N seconds with zero active connections. 0 (default)
disables.
.TP
.BI \-\-db " DATABASE"
SQLite database file; default is in-memory (shown as
.IR db=<none> ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on clean shutdown (including timeout-triggered shutdown).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a self-reaping server for a scripted session:
.PP
.EX
$ sock=$(dql server --socket-idle-timeout 30 | head -1)
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dql (1),
.BR dql-target (1)
